# Citation metadata read by GitHub's "Cite this repository" button and by
# Zenodo. Keep `version` and `date-released` in step with the crate release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use tellegen in your work, please cite the DXConf '26 paper below
  and, where the software itself matters, the release you used.
type: software
title: tellegen
abstract: >-
  Interactive power flow and optimal power flow in the browser. The Rust
  engine, its case parsers and solvers compile to WebAssembly; demand and
  rating edits preview through sensitivities and commit as exact re-solves,
  and case data never leaves the device.
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-09-23
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/eigenergy/tellegen
url: https://tellegen.dev
keywords:
  - power flow
  - optimal power flow
  - WebAssembly
  - interactive simulation
  - sensitivity analysis
  - multiconductor power flow
  - WebMCP
